ROBLOX luaL_loadprotected + protReader in lauxlib.c, loadstring routed through it; adds a stand-in
header (RbxProtectedString.h) for the RBX declarations used. Needs boost 1.53 headers on the include
path (boost/scoped_ptr.hpp).

Justification (PLAYER bytes; iOS 10-29 names luaL_loadprotected 0x0082610c, protReader 0x008263a4,
luaB_loadstring 0x00826f88 calling RBX::ProtectedString::fromTrustedSource):
- luaL_loadprotected 0x00876140: std::string computed; ps.calculateHash(&computed) 0x0066f060;
  if (ps.getOriginalHash() 0x0066ef40 != computed) [msvcp90 operator!=]: sendStats 0x00de4764 |= 0x200,
  lua_load(L, getS 0x00875970, {"" , 0}, name). Else a ProtectedLoad {index +0, ps +4, ch +8,
  scoped_ptr<MD5Hasher> +0xc, checked +0x10} is filled (stores index, checked, ps in that order),
  hasher.reset(MD5Hasher::create() 0x00652bf0) (swap-then-delete, no self-compare: boost scoped_ptr),
  hasher->addData(std::string(ps.getSalt() 0x0066ef10)) via vftable+8 with the string built before the
  hasher is loaded (implicit conversion), then lua_load(L, protReader, &pl, name).
- protReader 0x00875f10: feeds the previous char to vftable+4 addData(const char*, 1); a successful
  readUnprotectedChar 0x0066ef50 is the out-of-line tail (so the source tests the failure first);
  at the end, if index > 1 and not yet checked, compares a copy of getOriginalHash() with
  hasher->toString() (vftable+0x10); on mismatch sendStats |= 0x4000, checked = true and returns
  " ]]\r\n%" (0x00b80370) with its strlen.
- luaB_loadstring 0x008b0750: std::string(s, l) -> fromTrustedSource 0x0066f320 ->
  luaL_loadprotected -> load_aux, temporaries destroyed after load_aux (one full expression).
luaL_loadbuffer is no longer referenced by Lua and is absent from PLAYER (dead-stripped).

